IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg5, layer 1.
-- Sections 232 (delivery of notice; notice by electronic transmission) and 233 (notice to stockholders sharing an address).
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt of the Delaware Code Online (through 85 Del. Laws, c. 550).
-- It is not the official text. `-- src:N | ...` is line N of that file; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- What the two sections do. Section 232 says when a notice that the corporation gives to a stockholder is "given", by each way of giving it
-- (mail, courier, electronic mail, facsimile, a posting with separate notice, any other electronic transmission), when electronic notice is barred,
-- what the affidavit of the secretary proves, and fixes three chapter-wide definitions (electronic transmission, electronic mail, electronic mail address).
-- Section 233 lets one written notice serve stockholders who share an address, if they consent (or are deemed to).
-- Both sections are "without limiting the manner by which notice otherwise may be given effectively": so a date of NOTHING means
-- "this section does not make the notice effective by that way", not "the notice is ineffective".
--
-- Dates are whole days. The text speaks of the "time" a notice is given; the rules compare days (Fork F2 in NOTES.md).

§ `Section 232 -- the ways a notice is given`

-- src:972 | (1) If mailed, when the notice is deposited in the U.S. mail, postage prepaid;
-- src:973 | (2) If delivered by courier service, the earlier of when the notice is received or left at such stockholder’s address; or
-- src:974 | (3) If given by electronic mail, when directed to such stockholder’s electronic mail address unless the stockholder has notified the corporation in writing or by electronic transmission of an objection to receiving notice by electronic mail or such notice is prohibited by subsection (e) of this section.
-- src:978 | (1) If by facsimile telecommunication, when directed to a number at which the stockholder has consented to receive notice;
-- src:979 | (2) If by a posting on an electronic network together with separate notice to the stockholder of such specific posting, upon the later of:
-- src:982 | (3) If by any other form of electronic transmission, when directed to the stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(a)(1) to (3) (src:972-974); § 232(c)(1) to (3) (src:978-982)
DECLARE `dg5 s 232 Way a notice is given` IS ONE OF
    `by mail deposited in the U.S. mail with postage prepaid`
    `by courier service`
    `by electronic mail directed to the stockholder's electronic mail address`
    `by facsimile telecommunication directed to a number`
    `by a posting on an electronic network together with separate notice of that posting`
    `by any other form of electronic transmission directed to the stockholder`

-- src:971 | (a) Without limiting the manner by which notice otherwise may be given effectively to stockholders, any notice to stockholders given by the corporation under any provision of this chapter, the certificate of incorporation, or the bylaws may be given in writing directed to the stockholder’s mailing address (or by electronic transmission directed to the stockholder’s electronic mail address, as applicable) as it appears on the records of the corporation and shall be given:
-- src:975 | A notice by electronic mail must include a prominent legend that the communication is an important notice regarding the corporation.
-- src:976 | (b) Without limiting the manner by which notice otherwise may be given effectively to stockholders, but subject to subsection (e) of this section, any notice to stockholders given by the corporation under any provision of this chapter, the certificate of incorporation, or the bylaws shall be effective if given by a form of electronic transmission consented to by the stockholder to whom the notice is given. Any such consent shall be revocable by the stockholder by written notice or electronic transmission to the corporation. A corporation may give a notice by electronic mail in accordance with subsection (a) of this section without obtaining the consent required by this subsection.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(a) (src:971); § 232(a) last sentence (src:975); § 232(b) (src:976)
DECLARE `dg5 s 232 Notice given to a stockholder` HAS
    `the way the notice was given`                                   IS A `dg5 s 232 Way a notice is given`
    `the notice is directed to the address on the corporation's records` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the notice was deposited in the U.S. mail`             IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the notice was received by the stockholder`            IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the notice was left at the stockholder's address`      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the notice was directed to the stockholder by electronic transmission` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date of the posting on the electronic network`              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date of the separate notice of the posting`                 IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the electronic mail carries a prominent legend that it is an important notice regarding the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stockholder has notified the corporation of an objection to receiving notice by electronic mail` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stockholder consented to receive notice by that form of electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stockholder has revoked that consent`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the facsimile number is one at which the stockholder consented to receive notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date from which notice by electronic transmission is barred` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- src:987 | (e) Notwithstanding the foregoing, a notice may not be given by an electronic transmission from and after the time that:
-- src:988 | (1) The corporation is unable to deliver by such electronic transmission 2 consecutive notices given by the corporation; and
-- src:989 | (2) Such inability becomes known to the secretary or an assistant secretary of the corporation or to the transfer agent, or other person responsible for the giving of notice, provided, however, the inadvertent failure to discover such inability shall not invalidate any meeting or other action.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(e) (src:987-989)
-- Out of the stockholder's view: the corporation's two failed deliveries and the day the inability became known to the secretary,
-- an assistant secretary, the transfer agent or another person responsible for giving notice (the later of the two events).
-- The inadvertent failure to discover the inability does not invalidate any meeting or other action (see the next rule).
GIVEN `the corporation was unable to deliver 2 consecutive notices by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the inability became known to the secretary, an assistant secretary, the transfer agent or another person responsible for giving notice` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 232(e) the date from which notice by electronic transmission is barred` `the corporation was unable to deliver 2 consecutive notices by electronic transmission` `the date the inability became known to the secretary, an assistant secretary, the transfer agent or another person responsible for giving notice` MEANS
    IF `the corporation was unable to deliver 2 consecutive notices by electronic transmission`
    THEN `the date the inability became known to the secretary, an assistant secretary, the transfer agent or another person responsible for giving notice`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:989 | provided, however, the inadvertent failure to discover such inability shall not invalidate any meeting or other action.
-- NOTHING: the text protects only the inadvertent failure; it does not say what follows from a failure that was not inadvertent.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(e) (src:989)
GIVEN `the failure to discover the inability was inadvertent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(e) the meeting or other action is invalidated by the failure to discover the inability` `the failure to discover the inability was inadvertent` MEANS
    IF `the failure to discover the inability was inadvertent`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Is a notice that was directed by electronic transmission on a given day caught by the bar of subsection (e)?
-- The bar runs "from and after the time" both conditions hold, so a day on or after the day it starts is barred.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(e) (src:987-989)
GIVEN n IS A `dg5 s 232 Notice given to a stockholder`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(e) the electronic transmission directed on the date is barred` n d MEANS
    CONSIDER n's `the date from which notice by electronic transmission is barred`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST b   THEN d AT LEAST b

@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(a)(1) to (3) (src:972-974); § 232(b) (src:976); § 232(c)(1) to (3) (src:978-982)
GIVEN n IS A `dg5 s 232 Notice given to a stockholder`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 232(b) the date of a notice by electronic transmission that is allowed` n d MEANS
    IF   n's `the stockholder consented to receive notice by that form of electronic transmission`
     AND (NOT n's `the stockholder has revoked that consent`)
     AND (NOT (`s 232(e) the electronic transmission directed on the date is barred` n d))
    THEN JUST d
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(a)(2) (src:973)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE
      b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 232(a)(2) the earlier of the two dates` a b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN b
    WHEN JUST x  THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
        WHEN JUST y  THEN (IF x LESS THAN y THEN JUST x ELSE JUST y)

-- src:980 | a. Such posting; and
-- src:981 | b. The giving of such separate notice; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(c)(2) (src:979-981)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE
      b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 232(c)(2) the later of the two dates` a b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x  THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST y  THEN (IF x GREATER THAN y THEN JUST x ELSE JUST y)

-- The day on which a notice to a stockholder is "given", by the way it was given.
-- NOTHING: this section does not make the notice effective by that way (for example, a facsimile to a number the stockholder never consented to).
-- The notice may still be effective in some other manner: both (a) and (b) are "without limiting the manner by which notice otherwise may be given effectively".
-- src:971 | (a) Without limiting the manner by which notice otherwise may be given effectively to stockholders, any notice to stockholders given by the corporation under any provision of this chapter, the certificate of incorporation, or the bylaws may be given in writing directed to the stockholder’s mailing address (or by electronic transmission directed to the stockholder’s electronic mail address, as applicable) as it appears on the records of the corporation and shall be given:
-- src:976 | (b) Without limiting the manner by which notice otherwise may be given effectively to stockholders, but subject to subsection (e) of this section, any notice to stockholders given by the corporation under any provision of this chapter, the certificate of incorporation, or the bylaws shall be effective if given by a form of electronic transmission consented to by the stockholder to whom the notice is given. Any such consent shall be revocable by the stockholder by written notice or electronic transmission to the corporation. A corporation may give a notice by electronic mail in accordance with subsection (a) of this section without obtaining the consent required by this subsection.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(a) (src:971-974); § 232(b) (src:976); § 232(c) (src:978-982)
GIVEN n IS A `dg5 s 232 Notice given to a stockholder`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 232 the date on which the notice is given` n MEANS
    CONSIDER n's `the way the notice was given`
    WHEN `by mail deposited in the U.S. mail with postage prepaid` THEN
        IF   n's `the notice is directed to the address on the corporation's records`
        THEN n's `the date the notice was deposited in the U.S. mail`
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by courier service` THEN
        IF   n's `the notice is directed to the address on the corporation's records`
        THEN `s 232(a)(2) the earlier of the two dates` (n's `the date the notice was received by the stockholder`) (n's `the date the notice was left at the stockholder's address`)
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by electronic mail directed to the stockholder's electronic mail address` THEN
        CONSIDER n's `the date the notice was directed to the stockholder by electronic transmission`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST d  THEN
            IF   n's `the notice is directed to the address on the corporation's records`
             AND n's `the electronic mail carries a prominent legend that it is an important notice regarding the corporation`
             AND (NOT n's `the stockholder has notified the corporation of an objection to receiving notice by electronic mail`)
             AND (NOT (`s 232(e) the electronic transmission directed on the date is barred` n d))
            THEN JUST d
            ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by facsimile telecommunication directed to a number` THEN
        CONSIDER n's `the date the notice was directed to the stockholder by electronic transmission`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST d  THEN
            IF   n's `the facsimile number is one at which the stockholder consented to receive notice`
             AND (NOT n's `the stockholder has revoked that consent`)
             AND (NOT (`s 232(e) the electronic transmission directed on the date is barred` n d))
            THEN JUST d
            ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by a posting on an electronic network together with separate notice of that posting` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 232(c)(2) the later of the two dates` (n's `the date of the posting on the electronic network`) (n's `the date of the separate notice of the posting`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST d  THEN `s 232(b) the date of a notice by electronic transmission that is allowed` n d
    WHEN `by any other form of electronic transmission directed to the stockholder` THEN
        CONSIDER n's `the date the notice was directed to the stockholder by electronic transmission`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST d  THEN `s 232(b) the date of a notice by electronic transmission that is allowed` n d

§ `Section 232(d) -- electronic transmission, electronic mail, electronic mail address`

-- src:984 | (1) “Electronic transmission” means any form of communication, not directly involving the physical transmission of paper, including the use of, or participation in, 1 or more electronic networks or databases (including 1 or more distributed electronic networks or databases), that creates a record that may be retained, retrieved and reviewed by a recipient thereof, and that may be directly reproduced in paper form by such a recipient through an automated process;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(d)(1) (src:984)
GIVEN `it does not directly involve the physical transmission of paper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it creates a record that a recipient may retain, retrieve and review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a recipient may directly reproduce that record in paper form through an automated process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(d)(1) the communication is an electronic transmission` `it does not directly involve the physical transmission of paper` `it creates a record that a recipient may retain, retrieve and review` `a recipient may directly reproduce that record in paper form through an automated process` MEANS
        `it does not directly involve the physical transmission of paper`
    AND `it creates a record that a recipient may retain, retrieve and review`
    AND `a recipient may directly reproduce that record in paper form through an automated process`

-- src:986 | (3) “Electronic mail address” means a destination, commonly expressed as a string of characters, consisting of a unique user name or mailbox (commonly referred to as the “local part” of the address) and a reference to an internet domain (commonly referred to as the “domain part” of the address), whether or not displayed, to which electronic mail can be sent or delivered.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(d)(3) (src:986)
GIVEN `it consists of a unique user name or mailbox, the local part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has a reference to an internet domain, the domain part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `electronic mail can be sent or delivered to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(d)(3) the destination is an electronic mail address` `it consists of a unique user name or mailbox, the local part` `it has a reference to an internet domain, the domain part` `electronic mail can be sent or delivered to it` MEANS
        `it consists of a unique user name or mailbox, the local part`
    AND `it has a reference to an internet domain, the domain part`
    AND `electronic mail can be sent or delivered to it`

-- src:985 | “Electronic mail” means an electronic transmission directed to a unique electronic mail address (which electronic mail shall be deemed to include any files attached thereto and any information hyperlinked to a website if such electronic mail includes the contact information of an officer or agent of the corporation who is available to assist with accessing such files and information); and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(d)(2) (src:985)
GIVEN `it is an electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is directed to a destination that is an electronic mail address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(d)(2) the communication is electronic mail` `it is an electronic transmission` `it is directed to a destination that is an electronic mail address` MEANS
        `it is an electronic transmission`
    AND `it is directed to a destination that is an electronic mail address`

-- src:985 | (which electronic mail shall be deemed to include any files attached thereto and any information hyperlinked to a website if such electronic mail includes the contact information of an officer or agent of the corporation who is available to assist with accessing such files and information); and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(d)(2) (src:985)
DECLARE `dg5 s 232(d)(2) Matter sent with electronic mail` IS ONE OF
    `a file attached to the electronic mail`
    `information hyperlinked to a website from the electronic mail`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(d)(2) (src:985)
GIVEN m IS A `dg5 s 232(d)(2) Matter sent with electronic mail`
      `the electronic mail includes the contact information of an officer or agent of the corporation who is available to assist with accessing the files and information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(d)(2) the matter is deemed included in the electronic mail` m `the electronic mail includes the contact information of an officer or agent of the corporation who is available to assist with accessing the files and information` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `a file attached to the electronic mail` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `information hyperlinked to a website from the electronic mail` THEN
        `the electronic mail includes the contact information of an officer or agent of the corporation who is available to assist with accessing the files and information`

§ `Section 232(f) to (h) -- proof, enclosures, and the sections to which section 232 does not apply`

-- src:990 | (f) An affidavit of the secretary or an assistant secretary or of the transfer agent or other agent of the corporation that notice has been given shall, in the absence of fraud, be prima facie evidence of the facts stated therein.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(f) (src:990)
GIVEN `the affidavit is by the secretary, an assistant secretary, the transfer agent or another agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that notice has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(f) the affidavit is prima facie evidence of the facts stated in it` `the affidavit is by the secretary, an assistant secretary, the transfer agent or another agent of the corporation` `the affidavit states that notice has been given` `there is fraud` MEANS
        `the affidavit is by the secretary, an assistant secretary, the transfer agent or another agent of the corporation`
    AND `the affidavit states that notice has been given`
    AND (NOT `there is fraud`)

-- src:991 | (g) If a notice is given pursuant to paragraph (a)(1) or (a)(2) of this section, each document enclosed with the notice or annexed or appended to the notice shall be deemed part of the notice solely for purposes of determining whether notice was duly given under this title, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(g) (src:991)
GIVEN w IS A `dg5 s 232 Way a notice is given`
      `the document is enclosed with, annexed to or appended to the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(g) the document is deemed part of the notice for the purpose of deciding whether notice was duly given` w `the document is enclosed with, annexed to or appended to the notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `by mail deposited in the U.S. mail with postage prepaid` THEN `the document is enclosed with, annexed to or appended to the notice`
    WHEN `by courier service` THEN `the document is enclosed with, annexed to or appended to the notice`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:992 | (h) No provision of this section, except for paragraphs (a)(1), (d)(2) and (d)(3) of this section, shall apply to § 164, § 296, § 311, § 312, or § 324 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(h) (src:992)
DECLARE `dg5 s 232(h) Provision of section 232` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph (a)(1) of section 232`
    `paragraph (d)(2) of section 232`
    `paragraph (d)(3) of section 232`
    `another provision of section 232`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(h) (src:992)
GIVEN p IS A `dg5 s 232(h) Provision of section 232`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(h) the provision is one of those that still apply to the five sections` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `paragraph (a)(1) of section 232` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `paragraph (d)(2) of section 232` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `paragraph (d)(3) of section 232` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another provision of section 232` THEN FALSE

-- out of range: sections 164, 296, 311, 312 and 324 (pieces dg3, dg9, dg10)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 232(h) (src:992)
GIVEN p IS A `dg5 s 232(h) Provision of section 232`
      `the section under which the notice is given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(h) the provision of section 232 applies to the notice` p `the section under which the notice is given` MEANS
        (NOT (elem `the section under which the notice is given` (LIST 164, 296, 311, 312, 324)))
     OR `s 232(h) the provision is one of those that still apply to the five sections` p

§ `Section 233 -- one written notice for stockholders who share an address`

-- src:996 | (a) Without limiting the manner by which notice otherwise may be given effectively to stockholders, any notice to stockholders given by the corporation under any provision of this chapter, the certificate of incorporation, or the bylaws shall be effective if given by a single written notice to stockholders who share an address if consented to by the stockholders at that address to whom such notice is given. Any such consent shall be revocable by the stockholder by written notice to the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 233(a) (src:996)
DECLARE `dg5 s 233 Stockholder at a shared address` HAS
    `the stockholder consented to the single written notice`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stockholder is deemed to have consented to the single written notice under s 233(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stockholder revoked that consent by written notice to the corporation`          IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 233(a) (src:996)
GIVEN s IS A `dg5 s 233 Stockholder at a shared address`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 233(a) the single written notice is effective as to the stockholder` s MEANS
        (   s's `the stockholder consented to the single written notice`
         OR s's `the stockholder is deemed to have consented to the single written notice under s 233(b)`)
    AND (NOT s's `the stockholder revoked that consent by written notice to the corporation`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 233(a) (src:996)
GIVEN ss IS A LIST OF `dg5 s 233 Stockholder at a shared address`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 233(a) the single written notice is effective for all the stockholders at the address` ss MEANS
    all (GIVEN s YIELD `s 233(a) the single written notice is effective as to the stockholder` s) ss

-- "within 60 days of having been given written notice": the last day, notice date plus 60, is inside the period (Fork F3).
-- NOTHING: the 60 days have not yet run and the stockholder has not objected, so the text does not yet deem consent.
-- src:997 | (b) Any stockholder who fails to object in writing to the corporation, within 60 days of having been given written notice by the corporation of its intention to send the single notice permitted under subsection (a) of this section, shall be deemed to have consented to receiving such single written notice.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 233(b) (src:997)
GIVEN `the date the corporation gave the stockholder written notice of its intention to send the single notice` IS A DATE
      `the date the stockholder objected in writing to the corporation` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(b) the stockholder is deemed to have consented to the single written notice` `the date the corporation gave the stockholder written notice of its intention to send the single notice` `the date the stockholder objected in writing to the corporation` `the date on which the question is asked` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the stockholder objected in writing to the corporation`
    WHEN JUST o THEN
        IF o AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 60) `after` `the date the corporation gave the stockholder written notice of its intention to send the single notice`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN (`the date` (`period in days` 60) `after` `the date the corporation gave the stockholder written notice of its intention to send the single notice`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

-- out of range: sections 164, 296, 311, 312 and 324 (pieces dg3, dg9, dg10)
-- src:999 | (d) This section shall not apply to § 164, § 296, § 311, § 312 or § 324 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 233(d) (src:999)
GIVEN `the section under which the notice is given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 233(d) section 233 applies to the notice` `the section under which the notice is given` MEANS
    NOT (elem `the section under which the notice is given` (LIST 164, 296, 311, 312, 324))
